From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Korcan Hussein <korcan.hussein@collabora.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:40:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] vulkan: disable clustered subgroup ops on Adreno

Adreno's subgroupClusteredAdd/Max return wrong results on the Adreno 840
(the 830 does not report clustered support). The gated_delta_net shaders
already avoided them on Qualcomm, but quantize_q8_1_x4 still used its
clustered subgroup variant.

The kernel quantizes the activations for every integer-dot quantized
matmul with more than one column, so on the 840 all of them were
wrong: LoRA finetuning of Qwen3.5-0.8B started at loss 14.4 and went to NaN.

There are a number of issue reports in upstream of various issues
with the Adreno 840 there are most likely driver issues so
clear subgroup_clustered support for all qualcomm devices.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp | 14 +++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
index f1e165d79..0e3864c9a 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
@@ -4466,11 +4466,9 @@ void ggml_vk_load_shaders(vk_device& device, vk_pipeline requested) {
             const uint32_t S_V = gdn_sizes[si];
             GGML_ASSERT(is_pow2(S_V));
 
-            // Adreno's subgroupClusteredAdd returns wrong results in the gated_delta_net
-            // shaders (seen on Adreno 840); use the full-subgroup / shmem reduce path
-            // instead, which Adreno 830 (no clustered support) already takes and passes.
-            const bool clustered_ok = device->subgroup_clustered &&
-                                      device->vendor_id != VK_VENDOR_ID_QUALCOMM;
+            // subgroup_clustered is off on Adreno, whose clustered reductions are wrong (see
+            // ggml_vk_get_device); there the full-subgroup / shmem reduce path is used instead.
+            const bool clustered_ok = device->subgroup_clustered;
 
             uint32_t lanes_per_column;
             if (S_V >= 128u && clustered_ok) {
@@ -5107,6 +5105,12 @@ vk_device ggml_vk_get_device(size_t idx) {
 #endif
         device->subgroup_clustered = (vk11_props.subgroupSupportedStages & vk::ShaderStageFlagBits::eCompute) &&
                                      (vk11_props.subgroupSupportedOperations & vk::SubgroupFeatureFlagBits::eClustered);
+        // Workaround for Adreno's clustered subgroup reductions (subgroupClusteredAdd/Max) returning
+        // wrong results (seen on Adreno 840; the 830 does not report clustered support). Every kernel
+        // with a clustered variant falls back to a full-subgroup or shared-memory reduction.
+        if (device->vendor_id == VK_VENDOR_ID_QUALCOMM) {
+            device->subgroup_clustered = false;
+        }
 
         device->subgroup_ballot = (vk11_props.subgroupSupportedStages & vk::ShaderStageFlagBits::eCompute) &&
                                   (vk11_props.subgroupSupportedOperations & vk::SubgroupFeatureFlagBits::eBallot);
